** Over their response to a notrump opening (P12 batch 3)

The booklet gives no conventional defense to 1NT, so over the response we stay
natural: a suit bid is a natural overcall with a six-card suit (not in the suit
a transfer shows); over their natural 2NT a three-level suit is natural.
Everything else passes, and the partnership stops. (A lead-directing double of
an artificial response is standard practice too, but the notrump tables have no
continuation for the opener's side after it, so it is not written here: see
NOTES.md #P12.)

(1N)-P-(2C)-
2D = {prio:1} 8--15 hcp, 6+!d
  #STOP
2H = {prio:1} 8--15 hcp, 6+!h
  #STOP
2S = {prio:1} 8--15 hcp, 6+!s
  #STOP
#STOP

(1N)-P-(2D)-
2S = {prio:1} 8--15 hcp, 6+!s
  #STOP
3C = {prio:1} 10--15 hcp, 6+!c
  #STOP
#STOP

(1N)-P-(2H)-
3C = {prio:1} 10--15 hcp, 6+!c
  #STOP
3D = {prio:1} 10--15 hcp, 6+!d
  #STOP
#STOP

(1N)-P-(2S)-
3D = {prio:1} 10--15 hcp, 6+!d
  #STOP
3H = {prio:1} 10--15 hcp, 6+!h
  #STOP
#STOP

(1N)-P-(2N)-
cM = {prio:1} 10--15 hcp, 6+M
  #STOP
cm = {prio:1} 10--15 hcp, 6+m
  #STOP
#STOP

When the notrump opener doubles that overcall (a maximum, `notrump.bml`), the
notrump side has nothing more to say.

