** Over the response to their weak two-bid (P12 batch 3)

Over the 2NT inquiry (and opener's answer), and over a forcing new suit, the
direct seat acts as over the weak two itself (`defense.bml`), a little
stronger since the responder has shown values: a takeout double of their suit
with an opening hand and shortness, or a natural six-card suit with 11--16.
In the balancing seat after they stop in three of a suit the same calls.
(The tables name the weak twos, 2!d 2!h 2!s: a pattern `(2X)` would also
match the strong 2!c.)

