** Advancing a takeout double when the opener's partner bids (P12 batch 4)

`competition.bml` leaves these positions without rows (natural inference,
NOTES.md #C4). The booklet's advances of a takeout double assume the next hand
passed; when he bids instead, advancer is no longer forced, and a bid is a
"free bid" showing some values: a four-card major or a five-card minor at the
cheapest level with 6--11, notrump with a stopper, game in a major with 12+
and four cards. Over a redouble advancer bids his cheapest four-card suit even
with nothing (the double must be rescued), or passes for penalty with five
cards in their suit. With 12+ advancer bids 3NT with a stopper (13+) or
cue-bids the opener's suit, forcing. With less advancer passes. The doubler
passes the free bid (or advancer's pass) with the double's minimum, 12--16.
With more he cue-bids the opener's suit over the free bid, and doubles again
over advancer's pass (still for takeout: the double stays legal when they bid
on instead of passing, where the cue bid may not be); after either the auction
goes on naturally.

#CUT free-advance
4M = {prio:6} 12+ hcp, 4+M
  #STOP
3N = {prio:5} 13+ hcp, stopper
  #STOP
c\O = {prio:4} 12+ hcp
cM = {prio:3} 6--11 hcp, 4+M
  P = {prio:0} 0--16 hcp
    #STOP
  c\O = {prio:1} 17+ hcp
  #STOP
cm = {prio:2} 6--11 hcp, 5+m
  P = {prio:0} 0--16 hcp
    #STOP
  c\O = {prio:1} 17+ hcp
  #STOP
cN = {prio:1} 8--11 hcp, stopper
  P = {prio:0} 0--16 hcp
    #STOP
  c\O = {prio:1} 17+ hcp
  #STOP
P = {prio:0} 0--11 hcp
  P = {prio:0} 0--16 hcp
    #STOP
  D = {prio:1} 17+ hcp
#ENDCUT

(1X)-D-(1Y)-
#PASTE free-advance \O=X

(1X)-D-(1N)-
#PASTE free-advance \O=X

(1X)-D-(2X)-
#PASTE free-advance \O=X

(1X)-D-(2Y)-
#PASTE free-advance \O=X

(1Y)-D-(2X)-
#PASTE free-advance \O=Y

(1X)-D-(R)-
P = {prio:4} 5+X
  #STOP
cM = {prio:3} 4+M
  #STOP
cm = {prio:2} 4+m
  #STOP
#STOP

** Advancing a two-level overcall when the opener's partner bids a new suit (P12 batch 4)

As over their raise (`competition.bml`): a raise with three-card support and
6--12, a double with 11+ and four cards in their new suit (for penalty), and a
cue bid of the opener's suit with 13+ and support; otherwise a pass.

#CUT advance-two-level-overcall
3X = {prio:1} 6--12 hcp, 3+X
  #STOP
c\O = {prio:2} 13+ hcp, 3+X
D = 11+ hcp, 4+\u
  #STOP
#STOP
#ENDCUT

(1Z)-2X-(2Y)-
#PASTE advance-two-level-overcall \O=Z \u=Y

(1Y)-2X-(2Z)-
#PASTE advance-two-level-overcall \O=Y \u=Z

(1Y)-2X-(2N)-
3X = {prio:1} 6--12 hcp, 3+X
  #STOP
cY = {prio:2} 13+ hcp, 3+X
D = 11+ hcp
  #STOP
#STOP

A one-level major overcall raised by the opener's partner: with five-card
support and a weak hand advancer jumps to game (the booklet's preemptive
raise, one level higher).

(1X)-1M-(2X)-
4M = {prio:2} 0--10 hcp, 5+M
  #STOP

** Opener after a double of our opening and responder's bid (P12 batch 4)

`competition.bml` gives the responses to a double; opener's rebid is the
uncontested one: a raise of responder's suit with four cards (a jump with
16--18), a six-card suit rebid (a jump with 16--18), 1NT with 12--14 balanced
and 2NT with 18--19. After a 1NT response opener passes a balanced minimum and
rebids a six-card suit. Responder's new suit is forcing (`competition.bml`),
so opener never passes it: he also bids a new four-card suit at the one level
(12--18) or jumps in it (19+), raises to game with 19+, and otherwise rebids
his suit (12--18, the catch-all, usually six cards) or bids 3NT (19+). After a
minimum rebid responder, who would have redoubled with 10+, passes; after an
invitational one (16--18) or a new suit he decides naturally.

#CUT opener-after-double-response
2\R = {prio:3} 12--15 hcp, 4+\R
  #STOP
3\R = {prio:4} 16--18 hcp, 4+\R
4\R = {prio:4} 19+ hcp, 4+\R
  #STOP
3\S = {prio:2} 16--18 hcp, 6+\S
1N = {prio:1} 12--14 hcp, bal
  #STOP
2N = {prio:1} 18--19 hcp, bal
1Z = {prio:1} 12--18 hcp, 4+Z
jZ = {prio:3} 19+ hcp, 4+Z
2\S = {prio:0} 12--18 hcp
  #STOP
3N = {prio:0} 19+ hcp
  #STOP
#ENDCUT

1X-(D)-1Y-(P)-
#PASTE opener-after-double-response \S=X \R=Y

1X-(D)-1N-(P)-
2X = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 6+X
  #STOP
#STOP

Opener, when responder's natural 2NT over their two-level overcall is passed
round: 3NT with 14+, his six-card suit with a minimum, otherwise a pass.

1Y-(2X)-2N-(P)-
3N = {prio:2} 14+ hcp
  #STOP
3Y = {prio:1} 12--13 hcp, 6+Y
  #STOP
#STOP
